          "text": "If the earth suddenly shrinks to $\\frac1{64}$th of its original volume with its mass remaining the same, the period of rotation of earth becomes $\\frac{24}xh$. The value of $x$ is ______",
          "solution": "Volume $\\propto R^3\\Rightarrow R'=\\frac R4$. Angular momentum conservation: $\\frac25MR^2\\omega=\\frac25M\\left(\\frac R4\\right)^2\\omega'\\Rightarrow\\omega'=16\\omega$, so $T'=\\frac{24}{16}$ h. Hence $x=16$."
