          "correctAnswer": 2,
          "text": "A line segment $AB$ of length $\\lambda$ moves such that the points $A$ and $B$ remain on the periphery of a circle of radius $\\lambda$. Then the locus of the point, that divides the line segment $AB$ in the ratio $2:3$, is a circle of radius",
