          "solution": "Let there be $n$ couples. Choose $2$ men $\\binom n2$ ways; the $2$ women are chosen from the other $n-2$ women (excluding the wives of the chosen men): $\\binom{n-2}2$; the two teams can be formed in $2$ ways.<br>$\\binom n2\\binom{n-2}2\\cdot2=840$ gives $n=8$ ($28\\times15\\times2=840$). Total persons $=2\\times8=16$."
