    {
          "type": "numerical",
          "marks": 4,
          "negativeMarks": -1,
          "correctAnswer": 32,
          "text": "Let a common tangent to the curves $y^2=4x$ and $(x-4)^2+y^2=16$ touch the curves at the points $P$ and $Q$. Then $(PQ)^2$ is equal to ______.",
          "solution": "Tangent to the parabola: $y=mx+\\frac1m$. Its distance from the centre $(4,0)$ of the circle must be $4$: $\\frac{|4m+1/m|}{\\sqrt{1+m^2}}=4\\Rightarrow16m^2+8+\\frac1{m^2}=16+16m^2\\Rightarrow m^2=\\frac18$.<br>Take $m=\\frac1{2\\sqrt2}$: $P=\\left(\\frac1{m^2},\\frac2m\\right)=(8,4\\sqrt2)$. The foot of the perpendicular from $(4,0)$ to the tangent $mx-y+\\frac1m=0$ is $Q=\\left(\\frac83,\\frac{8\\sqrt2}3\\right)$.<br>$PQ^2=\\left(8-\\frac83\\right)^2+\\left(4\\sqrt2-\\frac{8\\sqrt2}3\\right)^2=\\frac{256}9+\\frac{32}9=32$."
    }
